@startuml Fluxo: Registrar Cliente
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plantuml-stdlib/C4-PlantUML/master/C4_Sequence.puml
autonumber

actor Client as "Consumidor HTTP"
participant API as "Fastify"
participant Route as "registry-routes"
participant Actor as "TokenActorResolver"
participant UseCase as "RegisterCustomer"
participant Repo as "CustomerRepository"
participant DB as "Drizzle / PostgreSQL"
participant Bus as "InMemoryEventBus"

Client -> API: POST /customers\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt>\n{cpfCnpj, name, email, tel}
API -> Route: valida headers e body com Zod
Route -> Actor: resolve e verifica CLIENTE_EDITAR
Actor --> Route: usuário ATENDENTE ou GERENTE
Route -> UseCase: execute(input)
UseCase -> Repo: findByCpfCnpj(CpfCnpj)
Repo -> DB: SELECT cliente por cliente_id
DB --> Repo: cliente existente ou null

alt CPF/CNPJ já cadastrado
    Repo --> UseCase: cliente existente
    UseCase --> Route: CustomerAlreadyExistsError
    Route --> API: erro de aplicação
    API --> Client: 409 CustomerAlreadyExistsError
else Novo cliente
    UseCase -> UseCase: cria CpfCnpj, Email e Telephone
    UseCase -> UseCase: Customer.register()
    UseCase -> Repo: save(Customer)
    Repo -> DB: INSERT INTO cliente
    DB --> Repo: sucesso
    UseCase -> Bus: publish(CustomerRegistered)
    Bus --> UseCase: concluído
    UseCase --> Route: {cpfCnpj, name, email, tel}
    Route --> API: 201 Created
    API --> Client: resposta JSON
end

note over API,DB
    A rota exige JWT Bearer válido e permissão CLIENTE_EDITAR.
    Validação Zod inválida retorna 400; token ausente/inválido retorna 401;
    usuário sem permissão retorna 403.
end note
@enduml
